lith_prefetch_budget_bytes 4.127829504e+09
# HELP lith_prefetch_committed_bytes Bytes prefetch has committed and nothing has consumed, which is exactly resident-unread PLUS queued-for-a-slot PLUS on-the-wire. Charged at DISPATCH, before the prefetch and S3 semaphores, so --inflight-bytes does NOT bound it: that bounds the wire, not the queue. This is not a resident-memory figure. At rest it equals lith_prefetch_unread_resident_bytes exactly; use that one, not this, to judge memory-tier pressure (#313, #320).
# TYPE lith_prefetch_committed_bytes gauge
lith_prefetch_committed_bytes 0
# HELP lith_prefetch_coverage_held_total Reads that made CONTIGUOUS progress and were denied a readahead window anyway, because coverage had not confirmed the access tiles. This rising while lith_prefetch_low_coverage_total stays flat is the signature of #316: concurrent readers of ONE object have their siblings' reads absorbed by the shared kernel page cache, so each handle advances in order yet looks punctate and never establishes -- measured at 243x slower with byte amplification of 1.001. Nothing counted this before: deEstablish() only counts an establishment that existed, and these handles are refused while still provisional.
# TYPE lith_prefetch_coverage_held_total counter
lith_prefetch_coverage_held_total 0
